+# [isambard3] meta vn2.2 -> vn3.2 via `rose app-upgrade`, to match the source this
+# env builds (2026.07.1). The whole vn2.2->vn3.0->vn3.1->vn3.2 macro chain runs, so
+# the ~900 lines of namelist churn below this comment are the tool's output, not a
+# hand port — deliberately, because a hand port is what made this suite look broken
+# before (see examples/science-suites/u-dt000/README.md).
+#
+# The three items this suite's science hangs on — held_suarez_sigma_b=0.97,
+# theta_relax_time_scale=100.0, wind_relax_time_scale=100.0 in
+# [namelist:external_forcing] — are Denis'. They survive the upgrade untouched, and
+# they are namelist fields only when the ice-giants forcing patch is applied to the
+# source (patches/optional/32-lfric_apps-ice-giants-forcing-patch.sh). Everywhere
+# else in LFRic they are hardcoded Fortran parameters, which is the
+# `Cannot match namelist object name held_suarez_sigma_b` this suite used to die on.
+#
+# NOT changed: the launcher. `RUN_METHOD=srun` sends the stock Met Office
+# launch-exe (LAUNCH_SCRIPT, upstream's) down a path that emits exactly
+# `srun $BIN_DIR/lfric_atm configuration.nml`, and XIOS stays attached
+# (XIOS_SERVER_MODE=False, upstream's value) — the same arrangement u-dr932 runs.
 meta=lfric-lfric_atm/vn3.2
 
 [command]
